    "problem": "Find the value of $(3\\mathbf{h}(t)-2\\mathbf{g}(t))^{'}$ at $t = 2$, if\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{h}(t) & =⟨2{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}t-3,\\hspace{0.222em}8+{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t) & =⟨{t}^{2}+2t,\\hspace{0.222em}8,\\hspace{0.222em}2{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "Differentiate componentwise: $h'(t)=\\langle4t,1,3t^2\\rangle$ and $g'(t)=\\langle2t+2,0,6t^2\\rangle$. Thus $$(3h-2g)'(2)=3\\langle8,1,12\\rangle-2\\langle6,0,24\\rangle=\\langle12,3,-12\\rangle.$$",
